# Arctic Wolves Video Companion Server
#
# No environment variables are required.
#
# All configuration is handled through the companion web UI and stored
# in an AES-256-CBC encrypted config file on the persistent Docker volume.
#
# ── Setup flow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Start the container:  docker compose up -d
#   2. Visit http://localhost:5100 — the setup page will appear.
#   3. Generate or paste an encryption key (use the same key as the main app
#      if you want matching PII encryption).
#   4. Go to Settings → click "Generate API Key" — copy the key.
#   5. Enter the generated key in the main app's Game Plan Settings →
#      Companion Server → API Key.
#   6. In the main app's RustFS settings, click "Push to Companion" to
#      send the S3/RustFS connection credentials automatically.
#
# If the container is updated, the encryption key persists on the volume.
# If the volume is lost, the setup page will appear again on first start.
#
# Storage paths (where videos live, where HLS output goes) are controlled
# entirely by the main application — it tells the companion exactly where
# each source file is and where to write the transcoded output.
